3. Existing Process
3.1 Overview

Before implementing the MHMR Data Processing Framework, data ingestion and processing lacked a standardized and scalable approach for managing daily incremental data. As the number of source tables increased, maintaining consistent processing, monitoring execution, and preserving historical data became increasingly challenging.

The existing process primarily focused on loading daily data without a unified framework for change detection, historical versioning, snapshot maintenance, or centralized operational logging. This resulted in increased manual effort for monitoring, troubleshooting, and recovering from failed executions.

